1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,753
Sticky, mushy or burnt rice at the bottom

2
00:00:02,763 --> 00:00:06,164
of the pot: almost everyone has been
there.

3
00:00:06,711 --> 00:00:08,939
The fix is simpler than you think.

4
00:00:09,486 --> 00:00:12,529
In seven steps, you'll cook fluffy rice
with

5
00:00:12,539 --> 00:00:16,103
separate grains, using only a pot, a lid

6
00:00:16,463 --> 00:00:19,272
and a stove, every single time.

7
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:21,957
And if a batch goes wrong, I'll show

8
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:23,324
you how to rescue it.

9
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,086
WikiTube.

10
00:00:25,447 --> 00:00:27,594
Whatever it is, here's how.

11
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:30,897
Rice goes wrong for a few simple reasons.

12
00:00:31,188 --> 00:00:34,545
Too much water, too much stirring, too
much

13
00:00:34,555 --> 00:00:37,898
heat, or a lid lifted at the wrong time.

14
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:40,698
Once you know the rules, rice is one

15
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:43,566
of the easiest foods you can cook, and

16
00:00:43,576 --> 00:00:45,514
it costs almost nothing.

17
00:00:46,316 --> 00:00:49,301
We'll use plain long-grain white rice as
our

18
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:51,948
example, and I'll tell you how to adapt

19
00:00:51,958 --> 00:00:55,963
for basmati, jasmine and brown rice along
the way.

20
00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:58,160
It is a method you will use for

21
00:00:58,170 --> 00:00:59,643
the rest of your life.

22
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,464
Here's what you need.

23
00:01:01,918 --> 00:01:03,925
Long-grain white rice.

24
00:01:04,379 --> 00:01:07,550
A medium pot with a tight-fitting lid,
since

25
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,522
the lid is the key to steam.

26
00:01:09,976 --> 00:01:11,287
A measuring cup.

27
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:15,153
A fine mesh strainer, or just a bowl.

28
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,253
A fork for fluffing at the end.

29
00:01:18,544 --> 00:01:20,772
And a pinch of salt, if you like.

30
00:01:21,319 --> 00:01:24,014
A kitchen scale is optional, because a
simple

31
00:01:24,024 --> 00:01:25,428
cup is enough.

32
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:27,034
Step one.

33
00:01:27,581 --> 00:01:30,053
Use a measuring cup to measure your rice,

34
00:01:30,146 --> 00:01:32,993
and remember the number, because the water
will

35
00:01:33,003 --> 00:01:34,093
be based on it.

36
00:01:34,895 --> 00:01:37,393
One cup of dry rice makes about three

37
00:01:37,403 --> 00:01:40,943
cups cooked, which feeds two to three
people.

38
00:01:41,908 --> 00:01:44,463
Choose a pot that suits the amount, since

39
00:01:44,473 --> 00:01:46,507
a pot that is too big dries the

40
00:01:46,517 --> 00:01:48,910
rice out, and a pot that is too

41
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,614
small boils over.

42
00:01:51,068 --> 00:01:54,271
A heavy-bottomed pot spreads the heat more
evenly

43
00:01:54,365 --> 00:01:56,082
and helps prevent burning.

44
00:01:56,884 --> 00:01:58,906
Take a moment to read the instructions on

45
00:01:58,916 --> 00:02:01,948
your package, because different varieties
of rice have

46
00:02:01,958 --> 00:02:03,606
slightly different needs.

47
00:02:04,756 --> 00:02:08,517
Measuring takes ten seconds and removes
the guesswork.

48
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:10,088
Step two.

49
00:02:10,635 --> 00:02:12,482
Put the rice in a strainer or a

50
00:02:12,492 --> 00:02:15,777
bowl, and rinse it under cold running
water,

51
00:02:15,905 --> 00:02:17,611
swishing it with your fingers.

52
00:02:18,761 --> 00:02:20,897
The water will start out milky.

53
00:02:21,258 --> 00:02:24,069
That cloudiness is surface starch, and it
is

54
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:26,748
what makes rice clump and turn gummy.

55
00:02:27,109 --> 00:02:29,467
Keep rinsing for about a minute, until the

56
00:02:29,477 --> 00:02:31,311
water runs mostly clear.

57
00:02:32,461 --> 00:02:35,630
Drain well, and shake off the excess
water.

58
00:02:36,594 --> 00:02:39,986
Rinsing matters most for basmati and
jasmine, while

59
00:02:39,996 --> 00:02:42,993
rice that is labelled pre-washed or
enriched should

60
00:02:43,003 --> 00:02:44,140
not be rinsed.

61
00:02:44,687 --> 00:02:46,741
Check the packet if you are unsure.

62
00:02:47,032 --> 00:02:49,855
Good rinsing is the difference between
restaurant rice

63
00:02:49,865 --> 00:02:51,663
and cafeteria rice.

64
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,279
Step three.

65
00:02:53,826 --> 00:02:57,357
For long-grain white rice, the classic
ratio is

66
00:02:57,367 --> 00:02:59,261
one cup of rice to one and a

67
00:02:59,271 --> 00:03:00,744
half cups of water.

68
00:03:01,894 --> 00:03:04,961
Basmati and jasmine are similar, around
one to

69
00:03:04,971 --> 00:03:07,408
one and a quarter or one and a half.

70
00:03:08,559 --> 00:03:11,611
Brown rice needs more, about one to two,

71
00:03:11,670 --> 00:03:13,387
and a longer cooking time.

72
00:03:13,748 --> 00:03:15,874
Add a pinch of salt, and, if you

73
00:03:15,884 --> 00:03:18,324
wish, a small knob of butter or a

74
00:03:18,334 --> 00:03:19,599
teaspoon of oil.

75
00:03:20,564 --> 00:03:23,581
Always check the instructions on the
packet first,

76
00:03:23,605 --> 00:03:25,172
since brands differ.

77
00:03:25,533 --> 00:03:28,622
The ratio is the secret, so measure it,

78
00:03:28,632 --> 00:03:30,222
and don't eyeball it.

79
00:03:30,769 --> 00:03:33,510
If you prefer softer rice, add a
tablespoon

80
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,190
more water, but never much more.

81
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:37,742
Step four.

82
00:03:38,033 --> 00:03:40,647
Put the pot on high heat, with the

83
00:03:40,657 --> 00:03:43,593
lid off, and bring it to a full boil.

84
00:03:43,954 --> 00:03:46,173
As soon as the water bubbles, give the

85
00:03:46,183 --> 00:03:48,994
rice a single stir to loosen anything
stuck

86
00:03:49,004 --> 00:03:52,254
to the bottom, and then don't stir it
again.

87
00:03:53,056 --> 00:03:56,564
Stirring rice releases starch, which makes
it creamy

88
00:03:56,574 --> 00:04:00,718
and sticky, great for risotto, but not for
fluffy rice.

89
00:04:01,171 --> 00:04:03,263
Be ready to move to the next step

90
00:04:03,273 --> 00:04:06,154
right away, because the water must not
boil

91
00:04:06,164 --> 00:04:07,893
away without the lid.

92
00:04:08,439 --> 00:04:11,503
It takes only a few minutes to get this
far.

93
00:04:12,050 --> 00:04:14,373
Use a timer on your phone, and don't

94
00:04:14,383 --> 00:04:16,496
walk too far from the kitchen.

95
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:18,205
Step five.

96
00:04:18,752 --> 00:04:21,131
Turn the heat down to the lowest setting,

97
00:04:21,584 --> 00:04:24,291
cover the pot with the tight lid, and

98
00:04:24,301 --> 00:04:26,750
set a timer for fifteen minutes.

99
00:04:27,297 --> 00:04:30,897
White long-grain rice usually needs
fifteen to eighteen

100
00:04:30,907 --> 00:04:34,099
minutes, brown rice around forty-five.

101
00:04:35,249 --> 00:04:38,012
Do not lift the lid during this time.

102
00:04:38,372 --> 00:04:40,824
The rice cooks in the trapped steam, and

103
00:04:40,834 --> 00:04:43,993
every peek lets heat and moisture escape,
which

104
00:04:44,003 --> 00:04:46,766
leaves you with hard, uneven grains.

105
00:04:47,312 --> 00:04:49,497
If your lid is loose, place a clean

106
00:04:49,507 --> 00:04:50,829
tea towel under it.

107
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:54,370
If your stove runs hot, use a heat
diffuser.

108
00:04:54,731 --> 00:04:57,682
A tight lid is non-negotiable, so choose a

109
00:04:57,692 --> 00:04:59,444
pot that closes well.

110
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,056
Step six.

111
00:05:01,417 --> 00:05:04,028
When the timer rings, turn off the heat,

112
00:05:04,203 --> 00:05:06,364
but keep the lid on, and let the

113
00:05:06,374 --> 00:05:08,231
pot sit for ten minutes.

114
00:05:08,684 --> 00:05:11,760
This resting time is as important as
cooking.

115
00:05:12,725 --> 00:05:15,513
The steam spreads evenly through the pot,
and

116
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,800
the moisture at the bottom is absorbed, so

117
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:20,502
the grains firm up and stop being sticky.

118
00:05:21,165 --> 00:05:23,222
Move the pot to a cool burner if

119
00:05:23,232 --> 00:05:25,555
you have an electric stove, because the
hot

120
00:05:25,565 --> 00:05:27,387
ring will keep cooking the bottom.

121
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:30,928
Don't skip it, even when you are hungry

122
00:05:30,952 --> 00:05:32,356
and dinner is waiting.

123
00:05:32,717 --> 00:05:35,307
Many people think this step is optional,
but

124
00:05:35,317 --> 00:05:37,766
it is where the texture is decided.

125
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,356
Step seven.

126
00:05:40,019 --> 00:05:42,644
Remove the lid and gently fluff the rice

127
00:05:42,654 --> 00:05:45,266
with a fork, lifting it from the bottom

128
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:46,694
and folding it over.

129
00:05:47,658 --> 00:05:50,469
A spoon crushes the grains, but a fork

130
00:05:50,479 --> 00:05:52,359
keeps them separate and light.

131
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,287
Serve it while it is hot.

132
00:05:54,949 --> 00:05:57,946
Leftover rice needs care, because it can
carry

133
00:05:57,956 --> 00:06:00,080
bacteria that survive cooking.

134
00:06:00,743 --> 00:06:02,997
Cool it within one hour, spread out on

135
00:06:03,007 --> 00:06:05,377
a tray if you can, then refrigerate it

136
00:06:05,387 --> 00:06:08,335
in a covered container and eat it within a
day.

137
00:06:09,299 --> 00:06:12,052
When reheating, make sure it is steaming
hot

138
00:06:12,062 --> 00:06:13,280
all the way through.

139
00:06:13,734 --> 00:06:17,089
A small splash of water helps in the
microwave.

140
00:06:17,633 --> 00:06:18,874
Rice went wrong?

141
00:06:19,839 --> 00:06:21,521
Most of it can be saved.

142
00:06:22,068 --> 00:06:24,020
If it is mushy, spread it on a

143
00:06:24,030 --> 00:06:27,210
tray to dry, or turn it into fried rice.

144
00:06:27,571 --> 00:06:29,639
If it is hard in the middle, add

145
00:06:29,649 --> 00:06:32,506
two or three tablespoons of water, cover
the

146
00:06:32,516 --> 00:06:35,304
pot, and steam it on very low heat

147
00:06:35,314 --> 00:06:36,579
for a few minutes.

148
00:06:37,381 --> 00:06:40,178
If the bottom is burnt, do not scrape it.

149
00:06:41,143 --> 00:06:43,649
Spoon out the good rice from the top.

150
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,312
Plain rice is only the start.

151
00:06:46,673 --> 00:06:48,938
Toast the dry rice in a little oil

152
00:06:48,948 --> 00:06:51,574
for a minute before adding the water,
which

153
00:06:51,584 --> 00:06:53,162
gives a nutty taste.

154
00:06:53,964 --> 00:06:56,613
Cook it in stock instead of water, or

155
00:06:56,623 --> 00:06:59,304
drop in a bay leaf or a cinnamon stick.

156
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:03,878
After fluffing, fold in lemon zest or
fresh herbs.

157
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:07,480
For fried rice, use rice cooked and
chilled

158
00:07:07,490 --> 00:07:08,731
the day before.

159
00:07:09,267 --> 00:07:11,739
A burnt pot is easy to avoid.

160
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:14,711
Use a heavy-bottomed pot with a tight lid,

161
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:17,207
and keep the heat as low as it will go.

162
00:07:18,009 --> 00:07:20,923
Set a timer, so you never have to guess.

163
00:07:21,725 --> 00:07:23,897
If you cook a larger amount, use a

164
00:07:23,907 --> 00:07:27,064
bigger pot and add a few extra minutes.

165
00:07:27,518 --> 00:07:30,097
If rice does stick, soak the pot in

166
00:07:30,107 --> 00:07:32,730
hot soapy water for half an hour.

167
00:07:33,267 --> 00:07:36,703
Now, the three mistakes that turn rice
into mush.

168
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:40,929
First, skipping the rinse, which leaves
too much starch.

169
00:07:41,475 --> 00:07:45,492
Second, adding too much water, or
measuring by eye.

170
00:07:46,294 --> 00:07:48,304
A little extra water is the most common

171
00:07:48,314 --> 00:07:50,031
reason for soggy rice.

172
00:07:50,392 --> 00:07:54,396
And third, lifting the lid or stirring
while it cooks.

173
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:57,777
Every peek lets out the steam, and every

174
00:07:57,787 --> 00:07:59,528
stir makes it sticky.

175
00:08:00,493 --> 00:08:03,525
Remember also that leftover rice should
never sit

176
00:08:03,535 --> 00:08:05,333
out on the counter for hours.

177
00:08:05,508 --> 00:08:08,015
Cool it quickly and refrigerate it.

178
00:08:08,567 --> 00:08:09,657
Let's recap.

179
00:08:10,111 --> 00:08:12,501
Measure your rice and pick the right pot.

180
00:08:12,955 --> 00:08:14,986
Rinse until the water runs clear.

181
00:08:15,347 --> 00:08:17,250
Use the right water ratio.

182
00:08:17,611 --> 00:08:20,454
Bring it to a boil and stir just once.

183
00:08:20,745 --> 00:08:23,763
Cover and simmer on low without peeking.

184
00:08:24,913 --> 00:08:27,072
Rest it off the heat for ten minutes.

185
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:30,868
And fluff it with a fork, then store
leftovers safely.

186
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:36,441
Seven steps, about thirty minutes, and
fluffy rice every time.

187
00:08:37,406 --> 00:08:41,668
The bonus sections cover rescuing rice,
flavor and

188
00:08:41,678 --> 00:08:42,896
burnt pots.

189
00:08:43,433 --> 00:08:46,601
That's how you cook rice perfectly on the
stove.

190
00:08:47,148 --> 00:08:49,912
If your rice turned out fluffy, subscribe
to

191
00:08:49,922 --> 00:08:54,507
WikiTube, because we publish a new how-to
every single day.

192
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:57,041
Tell us in the comments what you serve

193
00:08:57,051 --> 00:08:59,014
with your rice, and what you would like

194
00:08:59,024 --> 00:09:00,591
us to explain next.

195
00:09:01,045 --> 00:09:02,298
See you tomorrow.

196
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,548
That's WikiTube.

197
00:09:03,909 --> 00:09:05,615
Whatever it is, here's how.
